copisteria, https://github.com/kobimusic/copisteria

src/pipeline/copisteria/ is a JavaScript port of copisteria's reader
(commit c685f280914d91a694494588d9f6a376d7917eba, Copyright 2026 KobiMusic,
Apache License 2.0 — see LICENSES/copisteria-Apache-2.0.txt). The files were
changed from the original: translated from Python to JavaScript, the OCR-text
features left out, and fingerings.js added. The copista model weights
(kobimusic/copista-2m, kobimusic/copista-28m on Hugging Face, Apache-2.0) are
converted to ONNX by scripts/models/export_copista.py.

Verovio 6.2.0 (RISM Digital Center, https://github.com/rism-digital/verovio)
is used unmodified, as the npm package, under the GNU LGPL v3 or later: its
licence texts are LICENSES/verovio-LGPL-3.0.txt and the GPL v3 it builds on,
LICENSES/verovio-GPL-3.0.txt (the npm package ships neither). It is loaded as
its own file, so it can be replaced by another build of Verovio.

Third-party runtime libraries: ONNX Runtime Web (MIT), Verovio (LGPL-3.0),
Vue (MIT), coi-serviceworker 0.1.7 (MIT, Guido Zuidhof and contributors —
public/coi-serviceworker.js, LICENSES/coi-serviceworker-MIT.txt).

Page corners are found with DocAligner (DocsaidLab,
https://github.com/DocsaidLab/DocAligner, Apache License 2.0 — see
LICENSES/docaligner-Apache-2.0.txt): src/pipeline/capture/docaligner.js runs
its lcnet100 model, converted to ONNX.

The build writes THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt into the site: this notice, the
files in LICENSES/, and every npm package in the bundle (Vue, ONNX Runtime
Web, Verovio, jsPDF and svg2pdf.js among them) with its licence texts
(scripts/licenses/vite-plugin.mjs).

